   "summary": "Testers across every outlet agree the RM-Z250 is sprung far too stiff for typical 250 riders, the fork above all, and that softer springs or a revalve transform it. The engine pulls well low but flattens through the mid and top, it is the least powerful 250 on magazine dynos, and it has placed last in recent shootouts. With the suspension sorted it is rated among the best-cornering 250Fs, and its easy power suits novices and intermediates. The frame feels stiff on chop, the clutch slips when worked hard, and testers run the aggressive white coupler.",
